author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The static quality gate denies any src/cli or src/mcp import of an SDK module outside the transitive public export closure, seeded with a shrinking allowlist of the current ten; A negative control proves the new rule fails when a private SDK import is introduced; createExtensionCommandSdk, isRuntimeRecord and resolveStartTaskInProgressStatus are reachable from a public entry point or their consumers are relocated; The public surface snapshot and the consumer scan are joined by one check so the published surface and the consumed surface are compared rather than measured separately; The allowlist count is reported in the gate output so the ratchet direction is observable release over release"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: 88
resolution: Published SDK closure is now joined to CLI/MCP consumption by a shrinking fail-closed static ratchet.
expected_result: "CLI and MCP cannot add private SDK dependencies silently, and required SDK factories are publicly exported."
actual_result: "The gate computes transitive public exports, rejects new or stale private imports, reports seven remaining ratchet entries, and negative controls plus full coverage pass."
